cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EDRecon: An Explainable Reconnaissance Framework for Security Education"
message: "If you use this software in teaching or research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sinha
    given-names: Keshav
    name-prefix: Dr.
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science, University of Petroleum and Energy Studies (UPES), Dehradun, India"
repository-code: "https://github.com/keshavsinha/edrecon"
url: "https://edcatalyst.in"
abstract: >
  EDRecon is a reconnaissance framework built for security education. Unlike
  conventional scanners that emit bare observations, every finding carries a
  structured explanation of what was observed, why it matters, how it was
  detected, how to verify it manually, and how to remediate it. Explanatory
  content is decoupled from scanner logic in an editable YAML knowledge base,
  and authorisation is enforced structurally through a mandatory scope file
  with no bypass.
keywords:
  - security education
  - reconnaissance
  - penetration testing
  - explainable tooling
  - ethical hacking
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-16"
